{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.cyclicFaddeevPhi_dilog_periodic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.cyclicFaddeevPhi_dilog_periodic","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.lean#L137-L145","doc":"**Bonus — guard-free periodicity of the cyclic dilog** `Φ(x) = (x;ζ)_N⁻¹`:\n`Φ(ζ·x) = Φ(x)` (L2 `cyclicDilog_shift`, the reciprocal of the denominator's\nperiodicity). The full reciprocal boundary-trade law carries\nnonzero-denominator guards, so the dilog is not made a complete\n`CyclicFaddeevPhi` instance here; periodicity is its guard-free half, and it is\nthe closest form to the *invariance* the infinite Faddeev shift would want. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.cyclicFaddeevPhi_cyclic_carrier_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.cyclicFaddeevPhi_cyclic_carrier_eq","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.lean#L129-L135","doc":"The discharged carrier is concretely the finite polynomial `1 − x^N`\n(L1/L2 collapse `cyclicDenom_eq`) — evidence the fibre object is non-vacuous:\n`CyclicFaddeevPhi` is realised by an honest, explicitly-computable function, not a\nformal placeholder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.cyclicFaddeevPhi_cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.cyclicFaddeevPhi_cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.lean#L114-L127","doc":"**Discharge of the fibre-branch shift structure** (the payoff, closing G2).\n\nAt *every* primitive `N`-th root of unity `ζ` (`N > 0`), the finite q-Pochhammer\ndenominator `x ↦ (x;ζ)_N = ∏_{k<N}(1 − x·ζ^k)` is a genuine `CyclicFaddeevPhi`\ninstance: it satisfies the finite boundary-trade shift law\n(`cyclicDenom_shift_factor`, L2) and the exact N-periodicity\n(`cyclicDenom_shift`, L2). Unconditional, sorry-free — the fibre-branch analog of\n`PhiBProd.faddeevPhi_phiBProd_substrate`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.cyclicFaddeevPhi_periodic_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.cyclicFaddeevPhi_periodic_pow","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.lean#L102-L112","doc":"**Iterated periodicity**: `D(ζ^j·x) = D(x)` for every `j`. The single\n`ζ`-shift `periodic` iterated `j` times — the \"closes as a finite N-step\nrecursion\" statement (indeed period `1` in the `ζ`-scaling). Derived purely from\nthe class fields. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.CyclicFaddeevPhi.periodic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.CyclicFaddeevPhi.periodic","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.lean#L98-L98","doc":"Exact N-periodicity at the root of unity: the infinite-shift multiplier is\nabsorbed by the cyclic wrap-around. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.CyclicFaddeevPhi.shift_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.CyclicFaddeevPhi.shift_factor","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.lean#L95-L95","doc":"Finite boundary-trade shift law (finite analog of the Faddeev\n`Φ(q²x) = (1 + qx)Φ(x)` shift). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.CyclicFaddeevPhi.hζ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.CyclicFaddeevPhi.hζ","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.lean#L92-L92","doc":"`ζ` is a primitive `N`-th root of unity — the `|q| = 1` fibre datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.CyclicFaddeevPhi.hN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.CyclicFaddeevPhi.hN","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.lean#L90-L90","doc":"`N > 0` (the cyclic order is positive — the fibre analog of `FaddeevPhi`'s\n`0 < b.re`, i.e. a nondegenerate modular parameter). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.CyclicFaddeevPhi.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.CyclicFaddeevPhi.mk","kind":"ctor","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.CyclicFaddeevPhi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.CyclicFaddeevPhi","kind":"class","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiFibreBranch.lean#L69-L98","doc":"**Fibre-branch Faddeev-Φ shift structure** (the root-of-unity / `|q| = 1`\nanalog of `QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.FaddeevPhi`).\n\nA carrier `D : K → K` (think `D x = (x;ζ)_N`, the finite q-Pochhammer\ndenominator) at a primitive `N`-th root of unity `ζ` satisfies the two\n*multiplicative* shift laws that genuinely hold on the cyclic branch:\n\n* `shift_factor` — the **finite boundary-trade** law, the honest finite analog of\n  the Faddeev shift `Φ(q²x) = (1 + qx)Φ(x)`: scaling the argument by `ζ` trades\n  the bottom boundary factor `(1 − x)` for the top factor `(1 − x·ζ^N)`.\n* `periodic` — the **exact N-periodicity** `D(ζ·x) = D(x)`, in which the\n  `(1 + qx)`-type multiplier of the *infinite* Faddeev shift is **absorbed** by\n  the cyclic wrap-around (`ζ^N = 1` makes the top and bottom boundary factors\n  cancel).\n\nBoth fields carry genuine content (neither is `True` or an empty marker), per\nthe §3b-tax \"carrier must assert something\" rule. The class is discharged\nunconditionally by `cyclicFaddeevPhi_cyclic` below. ","signatureChunk":0}]}